</code></pre> <p>The components cannot live in <code>main.py</code> even though that is where the wiring is. The browser reaches them by dotted path, so they must sit in a module the server can import — a component defined next to the view is reachable as <code>main.counter</code>, but then the template has to say exactly that. Whatever you choose, the path in <code>{% component %}</code> and the entry in <code>root_components</code> must agree character for character. Nothing checks it for you: a mismatch emits markup that mounts an element which stays empty forever, and the failed import surfaces only as a server-side traceback on the websocket request.</p>
